  "functions": [
    "FUNC.PRICE"
  ],
  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "PRICE counts coupons n periods at once from maturity, uses derived dsc = E - A, and splits integer vs fractional powers",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, PRICE(settlement, maturity, rate, yld, redemption, frequency, [basis]) steps n coupon periods backward from maturity in one call (keeping the 29th/30th day instead of clamping February 28 into month-ends), sets dsc = E - A rather than the direct day count (diverging from COUPDAYSNC on bases 2 and 3), uses x87-stored binary exponentiation for integer exponents and exp(RN53(RN64(exp * ln(base)))) for fractional exponents, and divides redemption by its discount in x87. Of 9,153 full-bank rows, 9,103 match and 50 differ by 1 ULP.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131 and 16.0.20228 (9,103/9,153 full-bank and 120/120 pinned PRICE rows) and 16.0.20527.20088 in prefix_metadata (row 381).",
